{"fingerprint":"2ec1738dc31f740371180f5ba98e6efac76cef709788468606a900a6449d7750","path":"src/review_gauntlet/checkpoint.py","rule_id":"data-validation","content":"Race condition in `commit_latest_checkpoint`: between checking `dirty` / `staged_before` / `unstaged_before` and the subsequent `git add` + `git commit`, another process could modify the working tree or index. The error-recovery block attempts `git restore --staged` but only for `paths_to_stage`, leaving the index in a partially modified state if `git commit` fails after staging additional files. Consider using `git stash` or an index lock to make the check-stage-commit sequence atomic.","suggestion_code":"","existing_code":"    dirty = _get_all_uncommitted_paths(root)
    allowed_paths = _allowed_checkpoint_commit_paths(root, generated_files)
    staged_before = _split(_git(root, "diff", "--cached", "--name-only"))
    ...
    except subprocess.CalledProcessError as exc:
